Comments upon the three questions you ask:
Create a field in your data frame called "Effort" and assign the value 1000 to all rows in the data frame for that field
Nest decay rate:  the example of indirect surveys I suggested to you in my previous email (http://examples.distancesampling.org/Distance-mult/multipliers-distill.html) <http://examples.distancesampling.org/Distance-mult/multipliers-distill.html>   describes in detail (code included) how to produce an estimate of mean time to decay using logistic regression (code from Mike Meredith).  That example also provides citations to literature for you to examine.
18 months: I don't know enough about your survey design to answer that question.  Did you walk your transects only once, or monthly,...

